fields.text:
High risk of dehydration, electrolyte disturbance, AKI, and falls with aggressive prep;
sodium phosphate is contraindicated in older adults/CKD/heart failure. Overnight
regimens can disrupt sleep and increase falls.

– eGFR 20–50: 250 mg on alternate days OR 125 mg daily.
– eGFR <20: 250 mg on alternate days OR 125 mg daily (i.e. ~50% total weekly dose);
monitor LFTs and adverse effects.

NSAIDs accelerate GFR decline and worsen BP and oedema in CKD and heart failure;
paracetamol and non-renal opioids are preferred.
🟦 Diclofenac
